<title>SWITZERLAND: Nestle H1 group net rises 20 percent.</title>
<headline>Nestle H1 group net rises 20 percent.</headline>
<dateline>VEVEY, Switzerland 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>First six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			1,347	     vs 1,118</p>
<p> Trading profit		 2,459	     vs 2,444</p>
<p>Note - Full company name is Nestle SA. The consensus among analysts had been for profit of 1,360 million.  </p>
<p> Turnover			  28,444	    vs 26,926</p>
<p> Costs of goods sold	   14,962	    vs 14,280</p>
<p> Distribution expenses	  1,900	    vs  1,785</p>
<p> Marketing &amp; admin expenses   8,644	    vs  8,006</p>
<p> R&amp;D costs			    342	    vs    322</p>
<p> Restructuring costs		 97	    vs     80</p>
<p> Amortisation of intangibles     40	    vs	9</p>
<p> Net financing costs		417	    vs    465</p>
<p> Net non-trading expenses	  12	    vs     87</p>
<p> Profit before tax		2,030	    vs  1,892</p>
<p> Tax				    711	    vs    761</p>
<p>Net profit of consolidated</p>
<p> companies			  1,319	    vs  1,131</p>
<p>Share attrib to outside</p>
<p> interests			     83	    vs     96</p>
<p>Share of results of</p>
<p> associated companies	     111	    vs     83</p>
<p> Trading profit as pct of sales 8.6	    vs     9.1</p>
<p> Net profit as pct of sales     4.7	    vs     4.2</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
